# dependencies
# No trailing slash: with one, these match DIRECTORIES only, and a symlink
# named node_modules slips straight past them into a `git add -A`. That is
# exactly what happened in 704c613, which committed an absolute-path symlink
# pointing at one machine's checkout.
node_modules
app/node_modules

# build output
app/dist/
dist/

# wrangler / cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# local env (RevenueCat keys) — see app/.env.example
.env
.env.local
app/.env
app/.env.local

# capacitor native platforms
# app/ios/ IS committed — it carries the Xcode project, Info.plist tweaks and
# app icons, so a Mac only needs `npm install` (Capacitor 8 resolves native deps
# through SPM — there is no Podfile) to build. Its own app/ios/.gitignore
# excludes build output and the copied web assets.
# Android is still generated on demand with `npx cap add android`.
app/android/

# signing material. app/android/ is already ignored above, which covers the
# usual location — this is the belt-and-braces rule, because a leaked Play
# upload key is not something you can quietly rotate: recovering from it means
# asking Google to reset the key on the account.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
# ...and the Apple material the extension rules miss: a .cer or .pem is only a
# certificate (public), but a .key/.csr sitting beside one is the private half,
# and together they reconstruct the .p12. Rather than chase extensions, the
# whole folder is ignored and only its README survives — the same shape as the
# audio/ rule below. See secrets/README.md.
secrets/*
!secrets/README.md

# Steamworks SDK. A ~25 MB zip plus a 270-entry tree, redistributable binaries
# and a ContentBuilder that bakes in absolute paths; it is a versioned download
# from partner.steamgames.com, not source. tools/steamworks/README.md records
# which version to fetch and where it goes.
tools/steamworks/*
!tools/steamworks/README.md

# audio masters. The generated originals are the biggest thing in the project
# and are only needed when re-trimming; the PROCESSED assets under
# app/public/audio/ are committed and are what ships. audio/README.md is kept
# so the pointer to where the masters live survives in the repo.
audio/*
!audio/README.md

# misc
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
__pycache__/

# superpowers brainstorming scratch (visual companion mockups)
.superpowers/
